],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2025-10-08T15:08:33Z","updated_at":"2025-11-08T14:18:45Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: 4.5.stable.official\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7652) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-10400F CPU @ 2.90GHz (12 threads) - 15.91 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nCurveTexture appears to not record anything in its last pixel. Attached is an image of ColorRect with a shader that changes its shape according to a CurveTexture. The curve is set to be linear (from (0, 0) to (1, 1)), and appears to be missing interpolation data at the end.\n\n<img width=\"2560\" height=\"1381\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9ee22a9a-bfc1-4ce1-8553-a0a3cb3ac576\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nShader in MRP is set up to work with ColorRect with the size of 400 by 400 and CurveTexture width parameter of 200. The issue still persists with other parameters and offset will need to be adjusted but noticeability of this issue will vary\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[Curve Texutre Bug Report.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22780061/Curve.Texutre.Bug.Report.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111413/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111413/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}